id     = "shadow-lift-gaps"
about  = """A finding of round 8 (docs/decisions.md shadow-buffer): a surface's
buffer reserves its shadows' reach, which layout reads at rest, so when a
hovered card's lifted shadow sprang back the buffer shrank the same tick to the
resting shadow's reach and cut the shadow still drawn at nearly its lifted
size: flat at the buffer's edge for a frame as the pointer crossed the gap
between two cards, and at once on leave. Cards in a bar lift only their shadow
on hover; the pointer sweeps across them, gaps included, and leaves. The bar
now keeps the room its shadows are drawn in while they spring and shrinks once
they settle (`contain` shadow; eval/mutants/shadow-lift-gaps.patch reverts the
fix)."""
screen = { width = 400, height = 240, scale = 1.0 }
hz     = 60

=== shell.strand
bar Top {
  edge: top; height: 60; bg: #1e1e2e
  row { height: 60; pad: 0, 12; gap: 16; align: center
    for c in ["a", "b", "c"] key c {
      box { width: 80; height: 40; radius: 10; bg: #45475a; shadow: 0 2px 4px #00000066
        when hover { shadow: 0 12px 28px #000000aa }
      }
    }
  }
}

=== steps
pointer 5,30
rest
mark across
glide 5,30 -> 395,30 over 600
intend bar>row>box[0] changes
intend bar>row>box[1] changes
intend bar>row>box[2] changes
rest
mark leave
leave
rest
